-- title:
--   Uniform polynomial growth of unitary GL₂ Eisenstein series
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, $S_K$ a finite set of finite places of $K$, and $\xi_K$ a homomorphism from the full idele unit group to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ which is continuous, trivial on the image of $K^\times$, and of modulus $\|z\|^{w}$ for a fixed real $w$, where $\|\cdot\|$ is the idele norm given by the module character of the adele ring; let $N$ be an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_K$ all of whose prime divisors lie in $S_K$, and $\mathrm{tys}_K$ a family assigning to each infinite place finitely many finite-dimensional representations of the row-isometry group of the corresponding completion. Write $\alpha_m$ for the positive real character attached to the module character. The assertion is: for every compact $\Omega\subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ there are $C>0$ and $A\in\mathbb{N}$, depending only on these data, such that the following bound holds for all further data. Those data are: positivity of $\alpha_m$; characters $\mu,\nu$ of the ideles that are continuous, unitary and trivial on $K^\times$, with $\mu(z)\nu(z)\|z\|^{w}=\xi_K(z)$; real parameters $\tau^\mu_v,\tau^\nu_v$ describing the local components of $\mu,\nu$ on positive real elements at each infinite place $v$ as $\|\cdot\|^{i\tau_v}$, and integers $m^\mu_v,m^\nu_v$ describing them on norm-one elements as the $m_v$-th power; a family $s\mapsto\psi_s$ of functions on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ such that each $\psi_s$ transforms under the adelic Borel by $\mu\alpha_m^{s+1/2}$ on the first diagonal entry and $\nu\alpha_m^{-(s+1/2)}$ on the second, is archimedean-$K$-finite and $K_f$-smooth, the family being jointly continuous in $(s,g)$, holomorphic in $s$, with all right translates by the row-isometry group at each infinite place lying in one fixed finite-dimensional space, flat ($\psi_s=\psi_0$ on the adelic maximal compact), right invariant under the intersection of the principal level $N$ with the finite adelic subgroup, lying in the type-cut submodule for $\mathrm{tys}_K$, and normalised by $\int_{\mathbf{K}}\|\psi_0\|^2\le 1$ for the Haar measure on the maximal compact; finally an open preconnected $O_\psi\subseteq\mathbb{C}$ containing the imaginary axis and the half-plane $\operatorname{Re}s>1/2$, and functions $E_\psi,N_\psi$ analytic on a neighbourhood of $O_\psi$ in $s$ for each $g$ and jointly continuous on $O_\psi\times\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, such that for $\operatorname{Re}s>1/2$ one has the Bruhat expansion $E_\psi(s,g)=\psi_s(g)+\sum_{\xi\in K}\psi_s(w\,n(\xi)g)$ and $N_\psi(s,g)=\int_{\mathbb{A}_K}\psi_s(w^{-1}n(x)g)\,dx$ for the adelic additive Haar measure. Then for every $t\in\mathbb{R}$ and every $y\in\Omega$, $\;\|E_\psi(it,y)\|\le C\bigl(1+\sum_{v\mid\infty}(|t+\tau^\mu_v|+|t-\tau^\nu_v|+|m^\mu_v|+|m^\nu_v|)\bigr)^{A}$.
--
--   This is the locally uniform polynomial growth estimate for Eisenstein series on the unitary axis: the constants $C$ and $A$ are chosen in advance from the level $N$, the finite set $S_K$, the archimedean types and the compact set $\Omega$, and then serve simultaneously for all inducing characters $(\mu,\nu)$ compatible with the fixed central character $\xi_K$, all admissible flat holomorphic section families, and all points $it$ of the axis. It is the growth input for the spectral-side estimates used to construct and analyse the $L$-functions attached to such sections, being invoked by the statements on continuity and polynomial bounds of the pairings of axis continuations with cusp forms.
